hoto/135743986.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Montana Supreme Court has reaffirmed a previous ruling on a parenting plan modification initiated by Justin Aikins, who sought changes after his ex-wife moved a mere 10 miles away. The court concluded that minor increases in distance do not justify altering existing custody arrangements. Attempts at mediation were unsuccessful, and this decision establishes an important precedent regarding relocations and shared parenting in Montana.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-montana-father-sought-to-change-his-parenting-plan-after-his-former-wife-moved-arguing-it-made-visits-harder-the-state-supreme-court-ruled-that-10-extra-driving-miles-were-not-enough-to-reopen-the-arrangement/articleshow/135743986.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-montana-father-sought-to-change-his-parenting-plan-after-his-former-wife-moved-arguing-it-made-visits-harder-the-state-supreme-court-ruled-that-10-extra-driving-miles-were-not-enough-to-reopen-the-arrangement/articleshow/135743986.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T05:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135745971,imgsize-1415422.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A London financier lost his £2.6 million claim to his mother's Chelsea home]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135762603.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/london-financier-spent-over-20-years-living-in-his-mothers-3-85-million-chelsea-home-before-demanding-a-2-6-million-share-judge-rejected-his-claim-and-ordered-him-to-pay-85000-annually/articleshow/135762603.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/london-financier-spent-over-20-years-living-in-his-mothers-3-85-million-chelsea-home-before-demanding-a-2-6-million-share-judge-rejected-his-claim-and-ordered-him-to-pay-85000-annually/articleshow/135762603.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T04:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135762746,imgsize-1606770.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Oklahoma homeowner fined $8,528 as Supreme Court restores ban on his short-term rental business]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135746069.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A recent ruling by the Supreme Court has imposed a hefty fine of over $8,000 on an Oklahoma homeowner, Adewale Eniola Tawose. This decision reinstates the community's ban on short-term rentals after a legal tussle. Tawose's attempts to host guests led the homeowners association to act against him, reversing an earlier judgment that allowed his rental business, thus affirming the penalties and restrictions on such properties.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-oklahoma-homeowner-hosted-141-guests-during-36-short-term-stays-despite-neighbourhood-rules-after-a-lower-appeals-court-lifted-restrictions-the-state-supreme-court-restored-the-ban-and-upheld-8528-in-fines/articleshow/135746069.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-oklahoma-homeowner-hosted-141-guests-during-36-short-term-stays-despite-neighbourhood-rules-after-a-lower-appeals-court-lifted-restrictions-the-state-supreme-court-restored-the-ban-and-upheld-8528-in-fines/articleshow/135746069.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T04:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135746250,imgsize-2273507.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[An endangered leatherback turtle tried to nest on an Ecuador sidewalk before finding a quieter beach]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135716561.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Bella, a resilient leatherback turtle, made a remarkable nesting attempt in Ecuador, overcoming an array of challenges posed by artificial lighting. Her successful hatchling rates reveal a promising trend, indicating that leatherbacks are beginning to adapt to their new coastal environments. Conservation efforts are increasingly vital as these turtles face persistent threats, highlighting the urgent need to establish safe habitats for their upcoming nesting seasons.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/critically-endangered-leatherback-turtle-bella-makes-remarkable-nesting-attempts-in-ecuador-achieving-918-hatch-success-rate/articleshow/135716561.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/critically-endangered-leatherback-turtle-bella-makes-remarkable-nesting-attempts-in-ecuador-achieving-918-hatch-success-rate/articleshow/135716561.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T03:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135716895,imgsize-1014011.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Sheikh’s wife loses £8.3 million London mansion battle over Islamic gift claim]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135759740.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/billionaire-sheikhs-wife-loses-8-3-million-london-mansion-battle-after-claiming-her-husband-gifted-her-the-property-under-islamic-custom-leaving-the-home-exposed-to-his-80-million-business-debt/articleshow/135759740.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/billionaire-sheikhs-wife-loses-8-3-million-london-mansion-battle-after-claiming-her-husband-gifted-her-the-property-under-islamic-custom-leaving-the-home-exposed-to-his-80-million-business-debt/articleshow/135759740.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T03:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135760009,imgsize-133230.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indiana man loses pedal-pub injury lawsuit after appeals court upholds signed waiver]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135739532.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-indiana-man-joined-a-two-hour-pedal-pub-tour-drank-beer-and-fell-while-climbing-off-the-48-inch-high-seat-five-years-later-an-appeals-court-says-the-waiver-he-signed-prevents-his-negligence-claim/articleshow/135739532.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-indiana-man-joined-a-two-hour-pedal-pub-tour-drank-beer-and-fell-while-climbing-off-the-48-inch-high-seat-five-years-later-an-appeals-court-says-the-waiver-he-signed-prevents-his-negligence-claim/articleshow/135739532.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T03:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135739665,imgsize-618862.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Researchers turn discarded wind turbine blades into graphene-rich material for newer ones]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135716227.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Wind turbine blades are challenging to dispose of due to their long-lasting materials, which complicate recycling efforts. A research team from Tsinghua University has created a method for transforming discarded blades into silicon carbide and graphene. The process requires a rapid temperature increase using electrical pulses, which is effective in material recovery.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/electricity-turns-old-wind-turbine-blades-into-valuable-graphene-for-stronger-future-turbines/articleshow/135716227.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/electricity-turns-old-wind-turbine-blades-into-valuable-graphene-for-stronger-future-turbines/articleshow/135716227.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T02:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135716440,imgsize-1268814.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Woman's 32-day Airbnb stay turned into months-long legal battle in Washington]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135758706.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-woman-booked-a-washington-airbnb-for-32-days-after-a-fire-displaced-her-but-stayed-for-months-the-homeowner-offered-2500-and-two-months-of-free-rent-before-a-judge-ruled-in-her-favour/articleshow/135758706.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-woman-booked-a-washington-airbnb-for-32-days-after-a-fire-displaced-her-but-stayed-for-months-the-homeowner-offered-2500-and-two-months-of-free-rent-before-a-judge-ruled-in-her-favour/articleshow/135758706.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T02:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135758925,imgsize-1636623.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Texas man loses bid to keep gifted house as court awards wife $411,000 home and $175,000]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135731390.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Texas divorce appeal has shed light on property disputes between Joshua Peacock and Stephanie Ann Samples. The court confirmed that a rental property and a family business must be classified as community property. While Peacock asserted that the rental house was a gift from his father, he did not provide adequate proof.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-texas-man-said-his-father-gifted-him-a-rental-house-during-marriage-and-argued-the-family-used-car-dealership-was-worth-150000-a-court-upheld-giving-his-wife-a-411000-house-and-175000-divorce-payment/articleshow/135731390.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-texas-man-said-his-father-gifted-him-a-rental-house-during-marriage-and-argued-the-family-used-car-dealership-was-worth-150000-a-court-upheld-giving-his-wife-a-411000-house-and-175000-divorce-payment/articleshow/135731390.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T01:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135731445,imgsize-1811125.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists discovered a new orange-spotted fish which may already be on the brink of extinction]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135715977.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Researchers have unveiled Laimosemion laranja, a newly discovered species of killifish native to three isolated pools in Brazil. Facing grave threats from mining, deforestation, and urban pollution, this species is at risk of extinction. Through meticulous examinations and genetic analysis, scientists confirmed its uniqueness. To preserve this remarkable fish, they urge prompt protective measures to enhance its habitat and ensure its survival in the wild.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/newly-discovered-orange-spot-fish-in-brazils-amazon-faces-extinction-threat-from-mining-and-pollution/articleshow/135715977.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/newly-discovered-orange-spot-fish-in-brazils-amazon-faces-extinction-threat-from-mining-and-pollution/articleshow/135715977.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T01:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135716082,imgsize-95366.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Fake funeral fundraiser showed $16,000, but Atlanta family got nothing]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135767349.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-fake-fundraising-website-showed-16000-collected-for-a-13-year-old-atlanta-boys-funeral-his-family-said-it-never-received-the-money-and-a-funeral-director-stepped-in-to-cover-the-costs/articleshow/135767349.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-fake-fundraising-website-showed-16000-collected-for-a-13-year-old-atlanta-boys-funeral-his-family-said-it-never-received-the-money-and-a-funeral-director-stepped-in-to-cover-the-costs/articleshow/135767349.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T02:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135767689,imgsize-116780.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Texas appeals court overturns order barring granddaughter from family trust property]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135760717.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Texas appeals court has dissolved an order barring a granddaughter from coming within 500 feet of family trust property. The court found that the lower court had failed to set a trial date and specify the required security amount. However, the wider dispute over control of the Barbara Tolbert Revocable Trust and the family's inheritance claims remains unresolved.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-texas-granddaughter-was-barred-from-coming-within-500-feet-of-family-trust-property-as-relatives-fought-over-control-a-november-10-appeals-court-dissolved-the-restriction-but-left-the-inheritance-dispute-unresolved/articleshow/135760717.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-texas-granddaughter-was-barred-from-coming-within-500-feet-of-family-trust-property-as-relatives-fought-over-control-a-november-10-appeals-court-dissolved-the-restriction-but-left-the-inheritance-dispute-unresolved/articleshow/135760717.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T00:59:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135761775,imgsize-86520.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Swiss surgeon reclaims Guinness record with 3,200 heart-shaped objects after losing it in 2024]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135733832.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Diana Reser, a renowned Swiss heart surgeon, proudly holds the record for the largest collection of heart-shaped artifacts, now boasting 3,200 pieces. Her passion began during her medical studies, spurred by thoughtful gifts from loved ones. Reser's eclectic assortment features both decorative items and functional accessories, while she actively champions heart health awareness. Currently, she's on the lookout for a unique heart-shaped shower head to enhance her collection.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-swiss-heart-surgeon-who-lost-her-guinness-collection-title-in-2024-has-reclaimed-it-with-3200-heart-shaped-objects-diana-reser-has-spent-25-years-collecting-everything-from-art-to-household-items/articleshow/135733832.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/a-swiss-heart-surgeon-who-lost-her-guinness-collection-title-in-2024-has-reclaimed-it-with-3200-heart-shaped-objects-diana-reser-has-spent-25-years-collecting-everything-from-art-to-household-items/articleshow/135733832.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T00:56:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135733904,imgsize-1982853.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Stable Oxoboranes Isolated: Würzburg PhD pair trap rare bond; accident unlocks new chemistry]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135733857.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Two doctoral students at the University of Würzburg discovered stable oxoboranes, which contain a triple bond between boron and oxygen. Their findings emerged while studying reactions with diboracumulene and ketones, producing unexpected yellow and orange solids. The three new compounds can be isolated as crystalline solids and remain stable at room temperature. This breakthrough may allow greater exploration of their properties and reactions beyond previous limitations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/two-german-doctoral-students-were-studying-an-unrelated-reaction-when-their-flasks-filled-with-strange-orange-and-yellow-solids-and-they-had-accidentally-made-molecules-chemists-had-chased-since-the-1960s/articleshow/135733857.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/discovery/two-german-doctoral-students-were-studying-an-unrelated-reaction-when-their-flasks-filled-with-strange-orange-and-yellow-solids-and-they-had-accidentally-made-molecules-chemists-had-chased-since-the-1960s/articleshow/135733857.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T00:53:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135733905,imgsize-671266.cms"/></item></channel></rss>